# Everything not needed to build the backend image.
#
# This file is not housekeeping. `backend/.venv` alone is 88MB of an 89MB
# directory — without excluding it, every build copies a macOS-built virtualenv
# into a Linux image where it is both useless and enormous.

# virtualenvs — the image builds its own
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# secrets. The image gets its configuration from the environment, never from a
# baked-in file; a .env in an image is a credential you cannot rotate.
.env
**/.env
!**/.env.example

# the dashboard and its dependencies are not part of the backend image
dashboard/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# ML weights — downloaded on first run, and the backend doesn't do inference
*.pt

# perception's producer buffer: unsent events, machine-specific
*.bus-buffer.jsonl

# build and tool noise
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
.git/
.github/
**/.DS_Store

# docs don't change behaviour and invalidate the build cache when edited
docs/
*.md
!backend/README.md
